# Assumption Zero — environment variables
#
# Nothing here is required to run the demo. Assumption Zero works fully
# in DEMO MODE (deterministic static analysis + real code execution)
# with no keys configured at all. AI MODE is optional and only adds
# semantic analysis of arbitrary policies/repositories beyond the bundled
# demo target.

# --- AI mode (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# If set, analyzer/requirements.py can use the Anthropic API to interpret
# an arbitrary POLICY.md that doesn't use the ### REQ-n heading convention
# our bundled demo policy uses (see analyzer/ai_mode.py). This is real,
# working code, not a placeholder -- but nothing about the bundled demo
# depends on it: demo_target/POLICY.md always parses deterministically
# via the regex-based parser, so the live demo can never depend on this
# key being present, valid, or reachable. Never commit a real key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Demo application ----------------------------------------------------
# Override where the demo app's SQLite database file is written.
# Defaults to demo_target/backend/rapidrelief.db
RAPIDRELIEF_DB_PATH=

# --- Dashboard -----------------------------------------------------------
# The dashboard (apps/web/index.html) is served BY the analyzer API
# (apps/api/main.py) at http://localhost:8010 by default, so no separate
# base URL configuration is normally needed. If you serve the dashboard
# from somewhere else, its footer lets you point it at a different API
# base URL at runtime.
